From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:02:01 +0800
Subject: core/session: child sessions at their own location, and child forks

Upstream creates child sessions from parentID (plugin API and HTTP) at the
parent's location. This also lets a child name its own location (an octopi
worker in another directory), and session.fork accepts child: true to make the
copy a child of its source. Children get the built-in subagent treatment:
grouped under the parent, hidden from the session list, and reachable through
the parent's subagent navigation. The fork flag follows the maintainer draft
#51095 (Forked.child) so recorded events stay compatible if it lands.

Ocelot-Patch: core/child-sessions

